---
// One usage event, sent with curl: the same request and the same note on Home
// and Product. Customer acme-1 and the tokens meter are the ones "Send usage,
// get an invoice" makes.
import Code from './Code.astro';
import { doc } from '../site';
const text = `curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/v1/usage-events \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $HARDCOUNT_KEY" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\
  -d '{"event_name": "tokens",
       "external_customer_id": "acme-1",
       "quantity": 1200,
       "dimensions": {"model": "claude-sonnet-4.5", "token_type": "input"},
       "idempotency_key": "req-42:input"}'`;
---
<p class="prose">This is one usage event, sent with curl. <code>$HARDCOUNT_KEY</code> is the test key that <code>./quickstart.sh</code> prints. The customer <code>acme-1</code> and the <code>tokens</code> meter must exist first: <a href={doc('first-invoice.md')}>Send usage, get an invoice</a> creates them.</p>
<Code text={text} label="One usage event sent with curl" />
